From: Calculinux <noreply@calculinux.org>
Subject: [PATCH] spi: rockchip: raise sclk_out cap from 50MHz to 100MHz

The driver clamps ctlr->max_speed_hz to MAX_SCLK_OUT (50MHz), so no SPI
device can be clocked above that however high its spi-max-frequency.

With clk_spi0 at 187.5MHz, raising the cap lets the opt-in
lcd-spi-100mhz overlay run the PicoCalc ILI9488 at /2 = 93.75MHz instead
of /4 = 46.875MHz: ~49 instead of ~28 full frames/s. On its own this
patch changes nothing on the default DT, since the panel's 80MHz request
still lands on /4, and devices that ask for 50MHz or less (e.g. the
mmc-spi SD slot) keep their divisor.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [exceeds vendor-documented sclk_out limit]
Signed-off-by: Calculinux <noreply@calculinux.org>
---
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-rockchip.c
@@ -155,8 +155,12 @@
 #define RXDMA					(1 << 0)
 #define TXDMA					(1 << 1)

-/* sclk_out: spi master internal logic in rk3x can support 50Mhz */
-#define MAX_SCLK_OUT				50000000U
+/*
+ * sclk_out: spi master internal logic in rk3x is documented for 50MHz, but
+ * the RK3506 drives the PicoCalc ILI9488 well beyond that. Raise the cap so
+ * a device's spi-max-frequency above 50MHz is honoured instead of clamped.
+ */
+#define MAX_SCLK_OUT				100000000U
 /* max sclk of driver strength 4mA */
 #define IO_DRIVER_4MA_MAX_SCLK_OUT	24000000U

